# Antigravity GUI Installation & Setup Guide (English)

[한국어 가이드](./antigravity.ko.md) · [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest)

This guide walks you through installing, signing in, and running your first extraction using only the **Antigravity GUI** — no terminal commands or manual JSON editing required.

---

## Before You Start (1 Minute)

1. Sign in to your **Claire Bible** web interface.
2. Open **Account Settings** (`/settings/account`) and switch **Extraction mode** to **`Agent Client (client)`**.
3. Keep **MCP Settings** (`/settings/mcp`) open in your browser so you can copy the quick setup prompt or download `mcp_config.json`.

---

## Method 1 (Recommended): Paste Once in Antigravity Chat

You do not need to know hidden plugin folder paths or edit any JSON files.

1. On your Claire Bible **`/settings/mcp`** page, locate **Official Agent Marketplace (GitHub)** and click **Copy** next to **Antigravity quick setup prompt**.
   - If you are starting from GitHub directly, copy the prompt below and replace `<your-claire-server>` with your server hostname:
   ```text
   Install claire-antigravity (.zip) from the latest Release of
   https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}} into my Antigravity plugins
   folder, verify SHA256SUMS, write mcp_config.json inside the
   plugin folder for https://<your-claire-server>/mcp, and show the card.
   ```
2. Open the **Antigravity** app, click **`+ New Conversation`**, paste the prompt, and send it.
   - *About install-time permission prompts*: Antigravity may ask permission to download the archive and write outside your workspace (`~/.gemini/config/plugins/claire-antigravity`). Because installation runs once, selecting **`1 Yes, allow this time`** and clicking **`Submit`** is sufficient.
3. **Sign in to Claire Bible (OAuth 2.1)**:
   - Click **Sign in** on the **Claire Bible** plugin card shown in the chat reply, **OR**
   - Click **`Customizations`** in the left sidebar -> select **`Installed`** at the top right -> under **`Plugins`**, click **`Claire Bible`** (marked with an orange **`Setup required`** badge).
   - On `Customizations / claire-antigravity`, click **`Go to Accounts`** on the yellow **`Sign in required.`** banner (or select the **`Accounts`** tab), sign in in your browser, and approve the **`readonly`** and **`write`** scopes.

> **Note**: It is completely normal for **`MCP Servers 0`** (`No MCP servers yet. Use Add to browse the store.`) below `Plugins` to stay empty. Plugin-bundled MCP servers live inside **`Plugins -> Claire Bible`**, not under standalone `MCP Servers`.

---

## Method 2 (Point-and-Click): Manual File Setup

Use this method if you prefer downloading files yourself. **No text editor or JSON editing is needed.**

> **Important**: The `+` button next to `MCP Servers` opens the Marketplace store (`Use Add to browse the store.`) rather than a custom URL form. Place the downloaded `mcp_config.json` file inside the plugin folder as shown below instead.

### Step 1: Download the `.zip` Bundle and `mcp_config.json`
1. Open [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest) and download **`claire-antigravity-v{{VERSION}}.zip`**, then double-click to unzip the **`claire-antigravity`** folder.
2. On your Claire Bible **`/settings/mcp`** page, click **Download server config** to save **`mcp_config.json`**.
3. Move that **`mcp_config.json`** file directly inside the unzipped **`claire-antigravity`** folder (alongside `plugin.json`).

<details>
<summary>Creating mcp_config.json manually without opening /settings/mcp</summary>

Save `claire-antigravity/mcp_config.json` with your Claire Bible `/mcp` URL:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "claire": {
      "url": "https://<your-claire-server>/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

### Step 2: Move `claire-antigravity` Into Antigravity Plugins
Open the plugins folder for your OS and move the **`claire-antigravity`** folder inside. (If `plugins` does not exist yet inside `.gemini/config`, create an empty `plugins` folder first.)

- **macOS (Finder)**
  1. Choose **Go -> Go to Folder...** (`Command + Shift + G`).
  2. Enter `~/.gemini/config/plugins` and press **Return**.
  3. Drag the `claire-antigravity` folder into that window.
- **Windows (File Explorer)**
  1. Click the address bar at the top of File Explorer.
  2. Paste `%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\config\plugins` and press **Enter**.
  3. Move the `claire-antigravity` folder into that folder.
- **Linux (File Manager)**
  1. Open your Home folder and press `Ctrl + H` to show hidden folders.
  2. Open `.gemini` -> `config` -> `plugins` and move the `claire-antigravity` folder inside.

### Step 3: Sign In Inside the `Claire Bible` Plugin Page
1. In **Antigravity**, open **`Customizations`** in the left sidebar and select **`Installed`** at the top right.
2. Under **`Plugins`**, click **`Claire Bible`** (`Setup required`).
3. Click **`Go to Accounts`** on the yellow **`Sign in required.`** banner (or open the **`Accounts`** tab) and approve OAuth 2.1 (`readonly` and `write`) in your browser.

