## Handling Permission Prompts on First Run (`Allow using this MCP tool?`)

When you run your first Claire Bible prompt, Antigravity displays a permission prompt **`Allow using this MCP tool?`** for `claire-antigravity_claire/<tool_name>` (such as `claire-antigravity_claire/list_staged_sources`) with four options:

1. **`1 Yes, allow this time`** — Allow this single call only
2. **`2 Yes, and always allow in this conversation`** — Allow for the rest of this chat
3. **`3 Yes, and always allow`** — Always allow without asking again
4. **`4 No (tell the agent what to do instead)`** — Decline and instruct the agent otherwise

### What should I pick?
- **Personal-KB query and extraction tools (`list_staged_sources`, `claim_staged_source`, `get_staged_source`, `get_extraction_spec`, `resolve_entity`, `search`, `neighbors`, `submit_client_extraction`)**:
  - One extraction invokes 7–9 tools in sequence. Select **`3 Yes, and always allow`** and click **`Submit`** so extraction completes without pausing at every tool call.
- **Shared-KB contribution tool (`claire-antigravity_claire/kb_submit`)**:
  - Keep **`1 Yes, allow this time`** if you want an explicit confirmation before submitting documents to a shared knowledge base.
- **Reviewing or revoking saved grants**:
  - Open Antigravity **`Settings -> Permission Grants`** anytime to inspect or remove saved allowances.

---

## Verify Connection & Run Your First Extraction

Click any of the starter prompt chips on **`Customizations -> Installed -> Plugins -> Claire Bible`**, or paste one into a new chat:

- `List pending Claire Bible sources`
- `Extract and save pending Claire Bible sources`
- `Search topics in my Claire Bible knowledge graph`

Antigravity delegates raw source reading and extraction to the isolated `claire-extractor` subagent (Claire MCP tools only, zero shell/file tools) and commits validated results into your personal knowledge base.

