## FAQ & Troubleshooting

- **`MCP Servers` shows `0` (`No MCP servers yet. Use Add to browse the store.`).**
  - That is expected. MCP servers bundled inside a plugin live under **`Plugins -> Claire Bible`** (`MCP` and `Accounts` tabs), not in the standalone `MCP Servers` list.
- **`Claire Bible` shows `Setup required` and `Sign in required.`.**
  - OAuth 2.1 sign-in has not completed yet. Click **`Go to Accounts`** (or the **`Accounts`** tab) and sign in via your browser.
- **I cannot find the `.gemini` folder.**
  - Folders starting with `.` are hidden by default. Use `Command + Shift + G` in macOS Finder, paste `%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\config\plugins` into Windows File Explorer, or press `Ctrl + H` in Linux file managers.
- **`Claire Bible` does not appear under `Plugins`.**
  - Make sure there is no extra nested folder (`plugins/claire-antigravity/claire-antigravity/plugin.json`). The manifest must be at `plugins/claire-antigravity/plugin.json`.
- **Antigravity keeps prompting `Allow using this MCP tool?`.**
  - Choose **`3 Yes, and always allow`** and click **`Submit`** once per tool. Manage saved grants later in **`Settings -> Permission Grants`**.
- **How do I update to a newer version?**
  - Re-run Method 1, or unzip the new `.zip` over `plugins/claire-antigravity` while keeping your existing `mcp_config.json` and OAuth login.

---

<details>
<summary>CLI & Advanced Users (.tar.gz, SHA256SUMS verification, agy CLI)</summary>

1. Download and verify checksums:
   ```bash
   curl -fsSLO "https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/download/v{{VERSION}}/claire-antigravity-v{{VERSION}}.tar.gz"
   curl -fsSLO "https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/download/v{{VERSION}}/SHA256SUMS"
   sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing
   ```
   *(Use `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing` on macOS.)*
2. Extract and validate:
   ```bash
   mkdir -p ~/.gemini/config/plugins
   tar -xzf claire-antigravity-v{{VERSION}}.tar.gz -C ~/.gemini/config/plugins
   agy plugin validate --strict ~/.gemini/config/plugins/claire-antigravity
   ```
3. Write `plugins/claire-antigravity/mcp_config.json`:
   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "claire": {
         "url": "https://<your-claire-server>/mcp"
       }
     }
   }
   ```

</details>
